cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this template repository in your research, please cite it using
  the metadata below.

title: >
  Synthea-OMOP Study Development Template: An End-to-End Observational Study Pipeline for OMOP CDM
  using OHDSI HADES and Synthea Synthetic Data

authors:
  - given-names: "Adam P."
    family-names: "Johnson"
    name-suffix: "MD, MPH"
    affiliation: "Duke University School of Medicine, Department of Surgery"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3014-6372"
  - given-names: "Sasank"
    family-names: "Kalipatnapu"
    name-suffix: "MD"
    affiliation: "University of Massachusetts School of Medicine"
  - given-names: "Ayman"
    family-names: "Ali"
    name-suffix: "MD"
    affiliation: "Duke University School of Medicine, Department of Surgery"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-04-27"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Duke-Vascular-Informatics/synthea-omop-template"
url: "https://github.com/Duke-Vascular-Informatics/synthea-omop-template"

license: GPL-3.0

abstract: >
  A GitHub Template Repository providing an end-to-end pipeline for observational
  studies on an OMOP CDM v5.4 SQL Server database. Supports cohort characterization,
  prognostic modelling, and causal inference using the OHDSI HADES R toolstack.
  Includes synthetic data generation via Synthea for reproducible development and
  testing. Workflow steps cover environment setup, cohort definition, ETL to OMOP,
  data quality assessment (ACHILLES, Data Quality Dashboard), analysis, and
  manuscript-format report generation.
  Funding: Research reported in this publication was supported by the National
  Center For Advancing Translational Sciences of the National Institutes of Health
  under Award Number K12TR005435. The content is solely the responsibility of the
  authors and does not necessarily represent the official views of the National
  Institutes of Health.

keywords:
  - OMOP CDM
  - OHDSI
  - observational study
  - real-world data
  - clinical informatics
  - PatientLevelPrediction
  - CohortMethod
  - FeatureExtraction
  - Synthea
  - R

